  "integrity": "All selected response bodies verified against upstream byte count and Git blob SHA-1 (or LFS SHA-256 if present); per-input SHA-256 stored in the recordings table. Source files are at <sensor>/<object>/<pose>/<depth_directory>/real_sensor.csv or fem_sensor.csv.",
  "units_and_grading": "Native device_raw_fx/fy/fz and corrected_fx_N/fy_N/fz_N in N; device_raw_mx/my/mz and corrected_mx_Nm/my_Nm/mz_Nm in N·m. Fields use actual CSV names, which differ slightly from the data card. Both sides are from the same physical acquisition. No independently applied zero wrench or temperature is recorded; processing details do not identify causes of the differences. Simulation frame index does not establish physical contact onset.",
  "cleaning": "Keep archive order; ROS timestamps parsed as exact integers. Physical rows without a time and all 12 wrench components empty are counted separately. Rows sharing a timestamp can carry different wrench values. Keep every complete archived row for descriptive statistics, record duplicate times and flags for value changes. Distinct time labels are not automatically independent sensor observations. Rows and times are never aligned to a simulated trajectory by number. Camera filenames are counted within a file; no pixels analyzed and no contact inferred from a filename or controller phase.",
  "statistics": "For each physical file and each axis, compute the median, range and RMS around median of (raw minus corrected), in archive coordinates. Summary medians across condition files weight each condition equally. A nonconstant difference rules out modeling these recorded numbers as the same row minus one fixed offset; it does not identify any physical bias, thermal mechanism, time shift or reference wrench.",
